From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "lich.wang" <lich.wang@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:03:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] rpcd: listener: keep serving after a call fails

invoke_requested_procedure() returns an error for calls it cannot run,
such as a method hexagonrpcd does not implement, and the listener loop
then exited, ending the DSP's whole session. On SM8650 the sensor hub
calls apps_std method 36 (fopen_with_env_fd) once after the ADSP boots;
hexagonrpcd stopped there and the sensors only came up after the daemon
was started a second time.

Send the error back to the DSP with no output buffers and wait for the
next call instead. Free the input buffers of the failed call and do not
keep a pointer to output buffers that were already freed.
---
 hexagonrpcd/listener.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hexagonrpcd/listener.c b/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
index be5a15d..594c5fb 100644
--- a/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
@@ -621,12 +621,27 @@ int run_fastrpc_listener(int fd,
 
 		if (returned != NULL)
 			iobuf_free(n_outbufs, returned);
+		returned = NULL;
 
 		ret = invoke_requested_procedure(n_ifaces, ifaces,
 						 handle, sc, &result,
 						 decoded, &returned);
-		if (ret)
-			break;
+		if (ret) {
+			/*
+			 * The call failed before it ran (unsupported handle or
+			 * method, bad arguments, no memory): send the error back
+			 * with no output buffers and keep serving. Exiting here
+			 * would drop the DSP's whole session, which the DSP does
+			 * not expect for an optional method.
+			 */
+			if (decoded != NULL)
+				iobuf_free(REMOTE_SCALARS_INBUFS(sc), decoded);
+			decoded = NULL;
+			sc = REMOTE_SCALARS_MAKE(0, 0, 0);
+			n_outbufs = 0;
+			ret = 0;
+			continue;
+		}
 
 		if (decoded != NULL)
 			iobuf_free(REMOTE_SCALARS_INBUFS(sc), decoded);
